integrationWithRewardsWorld:
PRINCIPLE: rewards-world.js stays the single owner of state, rules, commits, HTML and sound decisions. The 3D stage only renders a view model and reports pointer events. One new adapter section (about 250 lines) keeps the 2D and 3D paths side by side.

NEW MODULE STATE: stage3d (the SLIsland3D instance, or null); use3D (null = undecided, true, or false for this session); coverCount; showtimeOn (remembered per device, wrapped in try/catch); musicOn.

render(): the starter grant and normalize flow are unchanged. Then draw(), then maybeBoot3D(), which is async and does nothing if a stage already exists, 3D failed this session, slNo3D is set or 2D is remembered. On boot success it creates stage3d = SLIsland3D.mount({reduced, user: {name, color: u.color, avatar: u.avatar}, on: {tapItem, tapPet, tapAvatar, tapLand, tapCell, dragStart, dragCell, dragEnd, ready, fail}}), then calls drawStage(). On ready, the 3D layer crossfades over the SVG.

draw(): the same skeleton, plus:
- HUD buttons '🌙✨ Showtime' (aria-pressed) and '🎵 Music';
- class .slw-is3d on .slw-stagewrap, and .showtime on .slw when Showtime is on;
- in 3D, skip stopPets()/startPets() and the phone scroll-centring.

drawStage(): becomes a dispatcher: use3D && stage3d ? drawStage3D() : drawStage2D(). drawStage2D() is today's body, unchanged and renamed. drawStage3D():
1. stage3d.attach(#slwStage);
2. stage3d.sync(islandView()), where islandView() = {
   - placed: w.placed, known ids only;
   - style: artState(w);
   - unlocked: C.unlockedRegions(w);
   - pets: owned pet records plus the active flag;
   - lit, mode, selectedUid;
   - placing: with the C.canPlace result;
   - newUids: window._slwNew;
   - anim: one-shot flags (unlock region, dropUid, styleDebut) };
3. builds the HTML anchors with today's classes and text (▶ PLAY tag, ✋ dot, NEW! badge, 🔒 lock-sign buttons with data-land, pet name bubbles) and passes them in with stage3d.setAnchors([{el, uid|pet|me|region, dy}]);
4. builds ul.slw-sr-list for keyboard users.
It must be cheap and idempotent, because draw() and drawStage() run after every commit.

TAPS: onObjectTap(e) is split so both the 2D click handler and on.tapItem call tapItem(uid, el).
- edit: selectedUid, then drawStage() + drawBar(). place: ignored.
- play: the same switch as today, but in 3D:
  - 'launch' → stage3d.act(uid, 'launch').then(() => launch(it.game));
  - 'home' → stage3d.act(uid, 'home') + openHome(); the sheet's onClose calls stage3d.act(uid, 'homeClose');
  - 'glow' → toggle lit[uid] (session memory, as today) + sync + 'star' or 'chip';
  - bounce, splash, swing, bubbles, spin, wave → stage3d.act(uid, it.act); the 3D act plays its own sounds through SLSound.
- Every tap gets the squish.
- fx(el, txt) and the CSS act classes are used only in 2D.

PETS AND AVATAR: startPets()/stopPets() run only in 2D. on.tapPet(id) → stage3d.emote('pet:' + id) plus the SLSound pet voice, replacing sfx('unlock'). on.tapAvatar → wave + finger-heart.

PLACEMENT:
- startPlacement(), placeKeys(), endPlacement() and cancelPlacement() are unchanged.
- drawPlacement() in 3D just calls stage3d.sync(islandView()); no .slw-cell buttons are drawn.
- New placeAtCell(x, y), factored out of the data-cx click handler, serves both the 2D cells and on.tapCell.
- on.dragStart(uid) (edit mode) → startPlacement(p.id, p.uid, false).
- on.dragCell(x, y) → update placing.x/y, then drawPlacement() + drawBar().
- on.dragEnd → confirmPlacement() if C.canPlace(...).ok.
- confirmPlacement() on success sets view.anim.dropUid, so the next sync plays the drop-in.
- storeSelected() calls stage3d.storeFx(uid, trayEl) before draw(). undo() is unchanged.

OVERLAYS: overlay() and celebrate() increment coverCount, and their close() decrements it; then stage3d.setCovered(coverCount > 0). Rendering pauses under sheets, and the last frame stays visible behind the backdrop. closeAllOverlays() resets the count.

SHOP AND SHEETS:
- cardHtml() adds class 'shine-' + SLIslandLook.shineLevel(it.price): price only, deterministic.
- Icons go through iconHtml(id, st) = <span class='slw-pc' data-pc=id data-pck=stateKey>SVG</span>. After each paint, SLPhotocard.fill(ov) swaps in cached PNGs progressively; the SVG stays when 3D is off.
- The same helper serves the goal bar, the storage tray, the confirm box, and the home and pets sheets.
- openItem(): #slwBig hosts SLPhotocard.turntable(host, id, st) when available, stopped by ov._close. '▶ Watch a preview' is unchanged until the games plan supplies a 3D autopilot preview.
- openHome(): a turntable of the player's own house that re-renders after each style pick.

afterPurchase():
- placeables: unchanged (placement, then the drop-in);
- land: draw() with anim.unlock = region, then stage3d.unlockLand(region).then(celebrate) (instant under reduced motion);
- attraction: NEW badge, drop-in, celebrate;
- style: the sync triggers the house rebuild and sparkle;
- pet: a spawn sparkle;
- price ≥ C.ECONOMY.confirmAt: celebrate() also fires the confetti cannons.
- When any celebration closes (including checkGoalReached's), call stage3d.showtime(true, {encoreMs: 8000}).
- Music ducks under fanfare, tada and applause via SLMusic.duck().

HUD:
- 'showtime' toggles showtimeOn, calls stage3d.showtime(on), switches the SLMusic context between island_showtime and island_day, and plays 'sting' + 'whoosh' (on) or 'chip' (off).
- 'music' → SLMusic.toggle(). The existing 'sound' mute also mutes music.

LIFECYCLE:
- onHide(): stage3d.suspend() stops the loop immediately; music fades out over 200 ms; a 30 s timer calls dispose() unless render() reopens the island first.
- onUserChanged(): closeAllOverlays() + render(), then stage3d.setUser(...) and a full sync. That cancels acts and encores, resets lit, and rebuilds the emoji face and the member-colour rim.
- launch(game): stage3d.suspend() and an SLMusic context switch before SLGames[game].start(cfg). cfg.onExit → stage3d.resume() + draw().
- onPointsChanged(): only adds the points-pill sparkle class.
- on.fail(reason): stage3d.dispose(), stage3d = null, use3D = false, drawStage() in 2D. Never a toast.

STAYS HTML:
- the whole HUD: Back to learning, ⭐ pill, goal bar, Shop, Games, Edit, Pets, Sound, Help, plus Showtime and Music;
- the edit bar and storage tray, and the placement bar messages;
- every sheet: shop, item detail, confirm, home, pets, info, intro, games list, time-limit dialogs;
- celebrations and toasts;
- all text labels (▶ PLAY, ✋, NEW!, lock signs, pet names), as projected HTML anchors;
- the keyboard list, the focus ring and the camera buttons.

THE CANVAS DRAWS: sky, sea, land, items, pets, avatar, the placement grid and ghost, particles and light effects.
